# faicheCourse — Conall's crash course in the garden (skyeGairdin)
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE. js/game/scenes/locations/skye/courseLines.js is
# GENERATED from it and overwritten on every compile. Edit here, not there.
#
#   node tools/dialogue/course.mjs tools/dialogue/drafts/faicheCourse.dlg --check
#   node tools/dialogue/course.mjs tools/dialogue/drafts/faicheCourse.dlg
#
# The LOGIC (when each slot is said, what the player must do) is in
# faicheCourse.js. This file is only the words.
#
# ── SYMBOLS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   == NAME   a lesson. The names are the code's; don't rename them.
#   =  NAME   a slot in the lesson: a moment the code says something.
#             Plain lines under it are Conall's (or the narrator's, in a
#             *Hint slot). One line per line on screen.
#   *  TEXT   a button the player presses, ending that slot's card.
#   >  TEXT   (under a *) what the player SAYS, if longer than the button.
#             Without one, the button's own words are shown as theirs.
#   <  TEXT   (under a *) what Conall says back.
#   %  TEXT   the Irish for the line directly above. For now each one
#             repeats the English (a placeholder: not shown as Irish, not
#             voiced). Write over it when the Irish is ready.
#   @value X  (under a *) what the button means to the course:
#               on     go on (the default)
#               again  have the lesson once more
#               wait   (meet only) not ready yet: no call to the mark
#   @goto S   (under a *) Conall's reply is slot S of this lesson (a card
#             of its own, which may have buttons of its own)
#   #         a comment
#
# A slot left out, or emptied, is simply not said. A slot ending in Hint (or
# called hint) is the NARRATOR: grey plain instructions, not Conall.
#
# Slots with buttons are cards. Others are cards or captions as the logic
# decides (captions are short, over the action).

@out js/game/scenes/locations/skye/courseLines.js

== meet
# He stands at the lake's edge watching the heron; the set piece opens when you walk up to him.

= look
The young warriors come here to fight 
% Tagann na n-Óglaigh anseo chun troid

as hawks of the sunburst
% mar seabhaigh an Gal gréine

= look2
 
But look well yonder
Ach féach tusa tháll
= look3

No light strikes 
% Ní bhuaileann solas 

nor trick of shadow deceives her fixation 
% ná scáth cleas ar a ghrinniú

little by little the heron becomes
%  an Corr de réir a chéile ag 

the enlightnement
% an léargais



= look4


an marú
% the kill

everything I could hope to teach
% Tá gach ceacht atá agam
is revealed by the heron
% múinte ag an gcorr
We begin.
% Tosaímid.

# a caption, as he calls you to the marked stone
= stand
Now. Stand here.
% Anois. Seas anseo.


# a card, once you are on it. {prince} is "prince" or "princess" by the champion
# (and the Irish, once there is some, likewise: prionsa / banphrionsa).
= stance
Stand as the heron stands.
% Seas ar nós na chorra

Not rigid. 
% Ní righin,

Not slack.
% ní bog

# a second card straight after
= stance2
Carry thy head as a {prince}.
% Iompair do cloigeann mar {prince} 
easy, unheld.
% go socair, gan srian
Let thine eyes be soft.
% Bíodh do shúile bog 
Let thy watching be boundless.
% Bíodh do fhaire gan teorainn 

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== space
# Bare-handed. He lunges at the tile you stand on (it reddens): step off.
# Then you shove him until he goes down on one knee.

= intro

Move.
% Gluais. 

# each time you get clear (one picked in turn)
= good
Again.
% Arís.

= mid
There.
% Sin é.


Now press me,
% Anois brúigh síar mé, 

until I am brought to my knee.
% go dtí go mbeidh mé ar mo ghlúin.

= shoveGo
Come, then. 
% Ar aghaidh, mar sin.

Knock me down.
% Leag mé.


# each shove that lands, before the last
= shoved
Again.
% Arís.

= after
There it is.
% Sin agat é.
Poor footing, half the battle.
% Droch-sheasamh, leath an chatha.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== sword
# You on the mark, he two tiles to your left. He throws you a practice sword.

# a caption, then the throw
= intro
Now.
% Anois.

# a card, once you've caught it (empty: none)
= caught
a chieftain unrisen is,
% Taoiseach suan is ea

The sword in its sheath 
% an claíomh sa truaill 

All his strength is there,
% Ann atá a neart, 

his fury, 
% a chaon-fhearg, 

the grief 
% an brón

he might bring upon his enemies.
% a d'fhéadfadh sé imirt ar a naimhde

Do not wake it without cause.
% Ná mhúscail é gan cuais.

# THE DRAW, DRILLED: draw / (his word on it) / put it away -- three draws, ending
# drawn. The salute is held back till the next lesson. The moon shows each gesture.
# the call, each time: the first line for the first draw, the second for the second, ...
# (the last one is used for any after)
= draw

Draw now.
% Tarraing anois.

# the call to put it away, between draws (one for each, as with the draws)
= sheathe
The returning of the blade is not lesser than the drawing.
% Ní lú é filleadh an chlaímh ná a tharraingt.

Sheathe it.
% Truaill é.

# said once it is away: one for each sheathing
= sheathed
 



# after each draw, the next of these (a caption); the last draw gets all that's left
= drawn


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== calls
# The salute. A card, then: draw, salute, again, again, again. No buttons:
# the blade stays out and the fatigue lesson follows straight on.

= intro
# In the order of the gesture, so that it can be said along with it: the hilt to the brow (the eyes: what he says to
# his own heart), the blade to the sky, the point down and out (the clean intent).

Now we salute.
% Beannaímid anois

Hilt to the brow.
% Dornchla chun an éadain. 



Blade to the sky.
% Lann chun an spéire.


Point to the earth.
% Rinn chun na talún.

Salute within, 
% Beannaigh istigh, 

salute in the heart.
% beannaigh sa chroí. 

I salute to say
% Beannaighím chun rá

What blood I spill here, 
% Cibé fuil a dhoirtim anseo,

I do so with open eyes.
% déanaim sin le lán thuiscint.



# the first call
= salute
Salute.
% Beannaigh.


# each call after the first (four salutes in all: faicheCourse.js SALUTES)
= again
Again.
% Arís. 

= enough
It will do.
% Is leor sin.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== fatigue
# He stands in as a target and turns every cut aside, till you're winded. "Stop."
# Then what it was for.

# captions: the blade stays out
= intro
Come against me. 
% Tar i mo choinne. 

Use thy full weight. 
% Bain úsáid as do mheáchan ar fad. 

Press hard.
% Brúigh go laidir.

Again.
% Arís.

Mark how I do not remain where I was.
% Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfanaim san áit a raibh mé.

= stop
Stop.
% Stad.


# a card, once you're winded and he's said "Stop." (no buttons); a second follows it
= after
The tide comes. 
% Tagann an taoide. 

It fills the low places. 
% Líonann sí na háiteanna ísle. 

It withdraws.
% cúlíann sé.


Thy breath is thy tide.
% Is í do anáil do thaoide.

Let it come. 
% Lig di teacht. 

Fill the low places.
% Líon na hísle. 

Withdraw.
% cúlaigh.



= after2
Let the head of the fearful one
% Bíodh cheann an chlaidhre 

fill with chatter.
% lán chainte.

Let the thoughts of the boastful one
% Bíodh smaointe an lán de lán

crowd with enemies.
% plódaithe le naimhde.



So rises the thought,
% Mar sin a thagann an smaoineamh, 

so falls the thought,
% mar sin  a imíonn sé.

yet the stone beneath the tide does not move.
% Ní chorraíonn an chloch faoin tíde.

Be thou the stone.
%  Bíse i do chloch.

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== dummy


# he draws and offers his salute; then yours
= salute
Raise thy sword now.
% Ardaigh do chlaímh anois.

# once you have saluted
= saluted
Good.
% Go maith. 
# and the work begins
= go
Hold it with sureness.
% Bíodh do greidhm cinnte. 

Strike at me,
% Tabhair buille dom.

swift,
% Bual go gasta.

without hesitation.
% Bual go cinnte.

Come at me now, 
% Tar

let me see what thou canst do.
% taispeáin dom cad atá ionat.


# captions, over the play: the first blow that would have landed
= landed
Thus. Dost thou see?
%  Mar sin. An léir duit?

= after
Look. 
%  Féach. 

Rooted as an oak. 
% Fréamhaithe mar dhair. 

No. No.
% Ní hea. Ní hea.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== feet
# He shows you first: back a step, in again, a cut; aside, in, a cut. Then you:
# a step, then a cut (tap the moon just after a step). Each pass needs a fresh
# step; a cut from where you stand, he turns aside. Five passes. He counts them:
# One. Two. Three. Four. (the fifth opens the card below). No narrator, no hints.

# said with each of his two cuts, as he shows you
= demo
Move thus.
%  Gluais amhlaidh.
And thus.
%  Agus amhlaidh.

= intro
Find the Daingean within thyself.
% Aimsigh an daingean ionat féin. 

It sits low, 
%Tá sé suite íseal,

below the navel. 
%faoin imleacán. 

Let thy weight descend to it.
%Scaoil do mheáchan síos chuige.

Motion begins there
% Tosaíonn an gluaiseacht ansin.

Not from the arm. 
% Ní ón géag. 

Not from the leg. 
% Ní ón cos.

Not from the clenching jaw.
% Ní ón giall fáscadh.

Move as thou dost strike, 
% Bual agus tú ag bogadh, 

for these are not two separate matters.
% óir ní dhá ábhar eagsúl iad. 


Woe to him 
% Is mairg an té 

who remains where the sword expects to find him.

% a fhanann áit a bhfuil claíomh ag súil leis.

= go
Move.
% Bog.

Strike. 
% Buail. 

Move again. 
% Bog arís. 

Let them reach for thee and find nothing, 
% Lig dóibh tú a lorg áit a raibh tú, 

while thy blade is already elsewhere.
% agus do lann in áit eile cheana féin.








# a cut from where you stand (now and then)
= still
 Move first.
% Bog ar dtús. 
Again. 
% Arís. 

Keep moving through the strike.
% Coinnigh ort ag gluaiseacht tríd an mbuille. 

Through it.
% Tríd.



# the first four passes, one line each (the fifth opens the card below)
= count
One.
% A haon.
Two.
% A dó.
Three.
% A trí.
Four.
% A ceathair.

= after
Five.
% A cúig.
Step to the side.
% Tóg céim ar leataobh.

Press and yield,
% Brúigh agus géill, 
This is the nature of the thing.
% Is é seo nádúr an ruda. 

buail agus tarraing siar. 
% strike and withdraw.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== drag
# Only now, near the end: drawing a line to walk. He draws one on the ground and
# walks it; then you draw yours, twice. (Till this lesson a drawn line does nothing,
# so it can't carry you off by accident in the lessons before.)

# a card; he sets off to draw his line when it is closed
= intro
Now. The movement.
% Anois. An ghluaiseact.

When thou must strike,
% Nuair a caithfear buille a thabhairt, 

do not think of striking.
% ná smaoinaigh ar an bhuaille.


Think of the movement.
% Smaoinigh ar an ghluaiseacht.

The strike is what the motion becomes.
% Is é an buille an ghluaisne féin.


# as he walks the line
= following
See it?
% An bhfeiceann tú?

= you
Now thy turn.
% Tusa anois.



# after the first line you draw
= good
Again.
% Arís.

= after
Good enough
% Sásúil


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== duel
# The last lesson: a bout. Draw a line at him; as you near him, time slows
# (bullet time). Land a blow in that slow, and his work is done.

= intro


there is a place
% Tá áit ann 


Between one motion
% idir gluaiseacht amháin


and the next,
%agus an chéad cheann eile.

= go
Now then.
% Anois maise.
En garde.
% Ar aire.

# a blow landed outside the slow (when you were not yet in the place between)
= won
Well struck.
% Buaille  maith. 

But there is a place between;
% Ach tá áit sa troid


thou hast not found it yet.
% nar aimsigh tú fós. 


# the blow landed in the slow: these, then `after`, as one card
# (NEW LINES: English placeholders)
= moment
There! Thou wert there.
% Mar sin! Bhí tú ann.
Strike as lightning.
% Buail mar thintreach.

= after
Thou hast the making of it.
% Tá an t-ábhar ionat.
Enough.
% Is leor sin.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== end
# The course is done: the green is open. Give Conall an `= intro` (a card) to
# say it himself; the narrator's line follows it either way.



# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== generic

# when you press "Once more"
= again
Again.
% Arís.

